WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.900 --> 00:00:06.800
Take a bag or basket outdoors to collect eight to twelve fallen leaves that look

2
00:00:06.800 --> 00:00:10.200
different. Thin paper and a peeled crayon are for rubbings.

3
00:00:11.033 --> 00:00:14.593
On a walk of 10 to 15 minutes, pick up fallen leaves only.

4
00:00:14.953 --> 00:00:16.933
Lay them out and look closely at the edges.

5
00:00:17.473 --> 00:00:19.153
Sort them one feature at a time.

6
00:00:19.513 --> 00:00:22.373
Then older children write yes or no questions to make a key.

7
00:00:23.133 --> 00:00:27.013
Colour is a poor feature, since one leaf can be green, red, or yellow.

8
00:00:27.553 --> 00:00:29.693
Edges, lobes, and leaflets work better.

9
00:00:30.467 --> 00:00:32.607
Do not touch any leaf made of three leaflets.

10
00:00:33.207 --> 00:00:36.187
Leave it on the ground, because poison ivy grows across Virginia.
